/// undecided: D-interp-backslash
/// Whether a string that contains a {placeholder} processes `\\` a second
/// time. The interpreter does (so a backslash prints differently depending on
/// whether the string has a placeholder); the VM does not.
x | 1
say("a\\\\b {x}")
say("a\\\\b")
say("""p="\\S" {x}""")
say("""p="\\S" """)
